<h2>Executive Summary</h2>

<p>Core thesis</p>
<p>Existing AI can already summarize information, surface anomalies, and provide suggestions. The next opportunity is to organize AI around the user's work — understanding ownership, prioritizing tasks, recommending actions, and helping close the loop.</p>

<p>Product strategy</p>
<ol>
<li>Start narrow: one persona, one workflow, and a small set of high-quality data domains.</li>
<li>Use the Supply/Demand Planner as the initial wedge, focused on operational exception resolution.</li>
<li>Use a personalized daily brief as the entry point, while making exception resolution the core value engine.</li>
<li>Build reusable platform primitives for context, tasks, actions, feedback, and governance.</li>
<li>Increase AI delegation only as quality and user trust are demonstrated.</li>
</ol>

<p>MVP outcome</p>
<p>Prove that an AI teammate can materially reduce the coordination work surrounding operational decisions while keeping humans in control of consequential actions.</p>
</section>

