<section>
<p>Slide 6</p>
<h2>Five Product Principles</h2>

<ol>
<li><strong>Task-oriented, not feature-oriented</strong><br>
Organize the experience around tasks, priorities, owners, and deadlines.</li>

<li><strong>Proactive, but selective</strong><br>
Optimize for signal and actionability rather than notification volume.</li>

<li><strong>Evidence before confidence</strong><br>
Show source data, business context, and explicit uncertainty behind important conclusions.</li>

<li><strong>Progressive delegation</strong><br>
Move from read → recommend → draft → approve → bounded autonomy as trust is earned.</li>

<li><strong>Governance by design</strong><br>
Permissions, auditing, data isolation, evaluation, and safety controls are platform primitives.</li>
</ol>
</section>

