<h2>Task Model: The Core Unit of the Experience</h2>

<p>The platform organizes information around a task rather than around individual alerts or source systems.</p>

<p>Task attributes</p>
<ul>
<li>Business object</li>
<li>Issue type</li>
<li>Priority</li>
<li>Owner</li>
<li>Due date / SLA</li>
<li>Business impact</li>
<li>Evidence</li>
<li>Recommended actions</li>
<li>Stakeholders</li>
<li>Status</li>
<li>Approval state</li>
<li>Outcome</li>
</ul>

<p>Example</p>
<p>Potential material shortage → affected order → priority → planner owner → supplier contact → recommended action → approval → follow-up → closure</p>

<p>Why this matters</p>
<p><strong>The task model becomes the common abstraction that allows the same AI capabilities to work across planning, procurement, logistics, and operations.</strong></p>
</section>

