<!-- Slide 13 -->

<section>
<p>Slide 13</p>
<h2>Entry Point: Personalized Daily Brief</h2>

<p>User expectation</p>
<p>“When I start my day, tell me what I need to care about, why it matters, and what I should do next.”</p>

<p>Every operating day, the AI teammate provides:</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Top priorities:</strong> a limited set of issues ranked by business impact and urgency</li>
<li><strong>Why it matters:</strong> affected orders, materials, quantities, timelines, and ownership</li>
<li><strong>Recommended actions:</strong> two to three concrete next steps</li>
<li><strong>Who to involve:</strong> relevant owners, stakeholders, and escalation paths</li>
<li><strong>Evidence:</strong> source data and supporting business context</li>
</ol>

<p>Feedback</p>
<p>Useful · Not relevant · Threshold too sensitive · Wrong owner · Already resolved</p>

<p>Guardrail</p>
<p>Only high-signal items should interrupt the user. Lower-confidence or lower-priority items go to an observation queue.</p>
</section>

