<section>
<p>Slide 14</p>
<h2>Core Value Engine: Exception-to-Resolution</h2>

<p>Six-step workflow</p>

<ol>
<li><strong>Detect &amp; group</strong><br>
Turn multiple related signals into a smaller number of task-level issues.</li>

<li><strong>Build context</strong><br>
Bring together relevant PO, inventory, shipment, capacity, SLA, ownership, and historical context.</li>

<li><strong>Explain impact</strong><br>
Separate confirmed facts from hypotheses and clearly identify uncertainty.</li>

<li><strong>Recommend next actions</strong><br>
Provide practical options, owners, and escalation paths.</li>

<li><strong>Coordinate</strong><br>
Draft email / IM communication, meeting agendas, and internal action items for human review.</li>

<li><strong>Track to closure</strong><br>
Monitor status, due dates, follow-ups, and lessons learned.</li>
</ol>

<p>Illustrative transformation</p>
<p>10 alerts → 3 task-level issues → 3 context packs → recommended actions → reviewed communications → tracked closure</p>

<p>Core promise</p>
<p><strong>Move from “people chasing alerts” to “tasks arriving with context and next actions.”</strong></p>
</section>

