<section>
<p>Slide 17</p>
<h2>Trust Model: Progressive Delegation</h2>

<p>AI autonomy should increase only as quality, trust, and governance are proven.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>L0 — Understand:</strong> retrieve, summarize, explain</li>
<li><strong>L1 — Recommend:</strong> prioritize and suggest actions</li>
<li><strong>L2 — Draft:</strong> prepare communications, reports, and action items</li>
<li><strong>L3 — Approve &amp; execute:</strong> execute approved actions within bounded workflows</li>
<li><strong>L4 — Bounded autonomy:</strong> automatically execute narrowly defined, low-risk actions</li>
</ul>

<p>MVP position</p>
<p>Primarily L0–L2, with limited L3 for internal action management where appropriate.</p>

<p>Core rule</p>
<p><strong>Automation follows evidence of trust; trust is not assumed from model capability alone.</strong></p>
</section>

