<section>
<p>Slide 18</p>
<h2>AI Quality, Safety, and Governance</h2>

<p>Quality evaluation</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Grounding:</strong> Is the response based on the correct source data and business context?</li>
<li><strong>Prioritization:</strong> Did the AI surface the right issues without creating unnecessary interruptions?</li>
<li><strong>Reasoning:</strong> Are confirmed facts separated from assumptions?</li>
<li><strong>Recommendation:</strong> Are suggested actions appropriate, actionable, and policy-compliant?</li>
<li><strong>Communication:</strong> Are generated drafts accurate and properly scoped?</li>
</ul>

<p>Safety controls</p>
<ul>
<li>Authorization enforced at retrieval and tool layers</li>
<li>Business content and tool outputs treated as untrusted input</li>
<li>Tool allowlists and parameter validation</li>
<li>Cross-vendor data isolation</li>
<li>Human approval for consequential actions</li>
<li>Full audit trail and source lineage</li>
</ul>

<p>Evaluation loop</p>
<p>Golden cases → Offline evaluation → Red team → Shadow mode → Human-in-the-loop pilot → Production monitoring</p>
</section>

