<section>
<p>Slide 21</p>
<h2>Pilot Design and Decision Gates</h2>

<p>Baseline</p>
<p>Approximately two weeks of workflow observation using time logs, system telemetry, and representative case samples.</p>

<p>Pilot comparison</p>
<p>Where practical, compare pilot users with a matched group or compare equivalent pre- and post-pilot workflows.</p>

<p>Quality assessment</p>
<p>Use structured human review for prioritization, recommendation quality, and evidence quality.</p>

<p>Qualitative feedback</p>
<p>Regularly interview users to understand why they accepted, ignored, or overrode AI recommendations.</p>

<p>Decision gates</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Scale:</strong> meaningful improvement in operational outcomes, sustained repeat usage, acceptable AI quality, and no material security or permission failures.</li>
<li><strong>Iterate:</strong> users engage with the system, but business impact or trust remains weak.</li>
<li><strong>Pause:</strong> quality, safety, permission, or governance thresholds are not met.</li>
</ul>

<p>Principle</p>
<p><strong>Predefine the evidence required to scale before the pilot begins.</strong></p>
</section>

